WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:05.687
Hello, everyone! I'm Ms. Emma. Welcome to Online Newspaper Class, level three.

2
00:00:05.987 --> 00:00:09.106
Hi! I'm Visal. Let's learn together!

3
00:00:09.406 --> 00:00:16.610
Unit twenty: Urbanisation and Housing. Today you will pack detail into noun phrases with several modifiers.

4
00:00:16.910 --> 00:00:19.794
Here is our lesson map. Let's start!

5
00:00:20.733 --> 00:00:24.071
Part one: words. You will learn eight new words.

6
00:00:24.917 --> 00:00:26.150
Urbanisation.

7
00:00:27.150 --> 00:00:31.321
Urbanisation means the growth of towns and cities as people move into them.

8
00:00:31.917 --> 00:00:34.682
Urbanisation has accelerated across Asia.

9
00:00:35.283 --> 00:00:38.017
Your turn. Say: Urbanisation.

10
00:00:40.867 --> 00:00:42.274
Urbanisation.

11
00:00:43.017 --> 00:00:43.704
City.

12
00:00:44.717 --> 00:00:47.134
City means a large and important town.

13
00:00:47.750 --> 00:00:50.597
The city grew rapidly after the new factory opened.

14
00:00:51.183 --> 00:00:53.522
Your turn. Say: City.

15
00:00:56.367 --> 00:00:57.124
City.

16
00:00:57.883 --> 00:00:58.629
Housing.

17
00:00:59.617 --> 00:01:02.057
Housing means buildings in which people live.

18
00:01:02.650 --> 00:01:05.741
Housing has become the biggest expense for many families.

19
00:01:06.350 --> 00:01:09.118
Your turn. Say: Housing.

20
00:01:11.967 --> 00:01:12.817
Housing.

21
00:01:13.583 --> 00:01:14.352
Rent.

22
00:01:15.350 --> 00:01:19.381
Rent means money paid regularly to use a home that belongs to someone else.

23
00:01:19.983 --> 00:01:22.354
Rent rose by ten percent last year.

24
00:01:22.950 --> 00:01:25.695
Your turn. Say: Rent.

25
00:01:28.533 --> 00:01:29.546
Rent.

26
00:01:30.283 --> 00:01:31.424
Infrastructure.

27
00:01:32.417 --> 00:01:36.796
Infrastructure means basic systems such as roads, water and power.

28
00:01:37.383 --> 00:01:39.789
Poor infrastructure slowed the city's growth.

29
00:01:40.383 --> 00:01:43.221
Your turn. Say: Infrastructure.

30
00:01:46.067 --> 00:01:47.323
Infrastructure.

31
00:01:48.083 --> 00:01:48.922
Planning.

32
00:01:49.917 --> 00:01:53.809
Planning means official decisions about how land and buildings are used.

33
00:01:54.417 --> 00:01:56.811
Careful planning reduced traffic jams.

34
00:01:57.417 --> 00:01:59.930
Your turn. Say: Planning.

35
00:02:02.767 --> 00:02:03.547
Planning.

36
00:02:04.283 --> 00:02:05.203
Migration.

37
00:02:06.217 --> 00:02:09.621
Migration means the movement of people from one place to another.

38
00:02:10.217 --> 00:02:13.029
Rural migration doubled the city's population.

39
00:02:13.617 --> 00:02:15.979
Your turn. Say: Migration.

40
00:02:18.833 --> 00:02:19.869
Migration.

41
00:02:20.617 --> 00:02:21.490
Affordable.

42
00:02:22.483 --> 00:02:25.725
Affordable means cheap enough for ordinary people to pay.

43
00:02:26.317 --> 00:02:28.548
Affordable homes are in short supply.

44
00:02:29.150 --> 00:02:31.605
Your turn. Say: Affordable.

45
00:02:34.467 --> 00:02:35.363
Affordable.

46
00:02:36.167 --> 00:02:40.050
Part two: dialogue. Let's listen to a conversation.

47
00:02:40.883 --> 00:02:47.715
Visal, a report describes 'a rapidly growing, densely populated coastal city'. Why are there so many words before 'city'?

48
00:02:48.817 --> 00:03:03.859
That is premodification. Several modifiers come before a noun and pack information into one phrase. The usual order is opinion, size, age, shape, colour, origin, material, then purpose.

49
00:03:04.950 --> 00:03:07.762
Is there a pattern for compound adjectives?

50
00:03:08.850 --> 00:03:25.007
Yes. Use a hyphen for modifiers made of two words: a fast-growing city, a low-income neighbourhood, a government-funded planning scheme. The noun stays singular: a ten-year plan.

51
00:03:26.117 --> 00:03:28.128
Why is it useful in urban news?

52
00:03:29.217 --> 00:03:40.620
It makes headlines and reports shorter and more precise: 'an affordable, well-connected housing development' says in one phrase what takes a whole sentence otherwise.

53
00:03:41.767 --> 00:03:43.337
Part three: grammar.

54
00:03:44.183 --> 00:03:49.376
Grammar focus: Complex noun phrases: several modifiers plus noun.

55
00:03:49.676 --> 00:03:50.932
Look at the pattern.

56
00:03:51.617 --> 00:03:56.867
A rapidly growing, densely populated coastal city needs better infrastructure.

57
00:03:57.783 --> 00:04:02.384
A government-funded ten-year planning scheme will build affordable homes.

58
00:04:03.283 --> 00:04:06.769
The low-income inner-city neighbourhood faces rising rent.

59
00:04:07.733 --> 00:04:17.781
Put several modifiers before a noun, with commas between same-type adjectives. Hyphenate compound modifiers (low-income, ten-year) and keep the noun in the singular.

60
00:04:18.517 --> 00:04:21.877
Be careful! Don't say: a ten-years plan

61
00:04:23.833 --> 00:04:26.030
Say: a ten-year plan

62
00:04:26.330 --> 00:04:28.574
Hyphenated modifiers stay singular.

63
00:04:29.367 --> 00:04:31.984
Part four: reading. Read and listen.

64
00:04:32.800 --> 00:04:33.917
Cities on the Move.

65
00:04:34.217 --> 00:04:37.331
Urbanisation is changing the shape of the modern world.

66
00:04:38.333 --> 00:04:45.743
Every year, internal migration brings thousands of job-seeking families into a fast-growing, densely populated city.

67
00:04:46.733 --> 00:04:52.959
Rising rent and a shortage of affordable housing push low-income residents into overcrowded outer districts.

68
00:04:53.967 --> 00:05:00.123
Careful planning and a long-term, government-funded infrastructure programme can keep a growing city liveable.

69
00:05:01.133 --> 00:05:06.871
Without them, even a prosperous, well-known capital becomes unfair and tiring to live in.

70
00:05:07.967 --> 00:05:12.003
Part five: quiz. Five questions. Are you ready?

71
00:05:12.850 --> 00:05:15.918
A city that is growing fast is a blank city.

72
00:05:16.218 --> 00:05:21.183
A, fast-growing. B, fast growings. C, fast-grown.

73
00:05:24.733 --> 00:05:26.803
The answer is A: fast-growing.

74
00:05:27.950 --> 00:05:30.635
A plan that lasts ten years is a blank plan.

75
00:05:30.935 --> 00:05:34.542
A, ten-years. B, ten year. C, ten-year.

76
00:05:38.100 --> 00:05:39.763
The answer is C: ten-year.

77
00:05:40.917 --> 00:05:44.089
Roads, water and power systems are called blank.

78
00:05:44.389 --> 00:05:48.205
A, migration. B, rent. C, infrastructure.

79
00:05:51.767 --> 00:05:54.451
The answer is C: infrastructure.

80
00:05:55.617 --> 00:05:57.314
Choose the correct phrase.

81
00:05:57.614 --> 00:06:04.031
A, a low-incomes family. B, a low-income family. C, a low incomes family.

82
00:06:07.567 --> 00:06:09.833
The answer is B: a low-income family.

83
00:06:10.983 --> 00:06:16.536
According to the reading, rising rent and a shortage of affordable housing push residents into…

84
00:06:16.836 --> 00:06:22.126
A, overcrowded outer districts. B, new capitals. C, empty cities.

85
00:06:25.667 --> 00:06:28.572
The answer is A: overcrowded outer districts.

86
00:06:29.767 --> 00:06:32.965
Part six: speaking. It's your turn to talk.

87
00:06:33.817 --> 00:06:36.397
What challenges does fast city growth create?

88
00:06:45.183 --> 00:06:46.707
Now listen to Visal.

89
00:06:47.007 --> 00:07:15.740
Fast city growth creates pressure on housing, transport, water and schools. Rents rise, traffic becomes heavy and poorer families may live in informal settlements without safe services. Pollution and noise can increase, and local governments often struggle to collect enough tax to build new infrastructure. Careful planning and affordable housing are needed so that growth benefits everyone, not only wealthy residents.

90
00:07:16.040 --> 00:07:17.761
Excellent answer, Visal!

91
00:07:18.650 --> 00:07:25.110
Great work! Now you can use eight new words and complex noun phrases: several modifiers plus noun.

92
00:07:25.410 --> 00:07:30.118
Today's value is community resilience. Stronger communities recover together.

93
00:07:30.418 --> 00:07:32.838
See you in Unit twenty-one. Goodbye!

94
00:07:33.138 --> 00:07:36.684
Thank you, Ms. Emma! Bye, everyone!

